{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('map.json')); m['version']=13\nnew_text=(\\\"the command value codec frames a value's length in a two-byte field on both sides, while the client's command size is configuration-driven; the three direct checks for claim C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire confirmed in scope that a 70000-byte value is written as 70013 bytes but decoded as 4464 bytes with 4477 consumed, that the command following such a value in the same buffer decodes to garbage (op 197, an arbitrary key and a 53198-byte value), and that decoding a real PreAccept carrying such a value panics with makeslice: len out of range, which the receiver's reader has no recover for. The default configuration's 1000-byte commands never reach the boundary, and what a participant does after a displaced stream is unread (S37-state-value-codec, S38-client-command-size, S22-replica-listener).\\\")\nfor i,o in enumerate(m['core_overview']['open_details']):\n    if o.startswith('the command value codec frames'):\n        m['core_overview']['open_details'][i]=new_text\n        break\nfor s in m['surfaces']:\n    if s['entry_point'].startswith('state/state.go value and command codec'):\n        s['reason']=(\\\"the value and command wire codecs frame every command a replica sends or receives; they carry no protocol decision, but the direct checks for claim C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire confirmed that a value beyond the two-byte length field is silently shortened while its bytes remain in the stream, that the next command decodes to garbage, and that a real PreAccept carrying such a value makes the receiver's decoder panic, which the default 1000-byte command size does not reach (S37-state-value-codec, S38-client-command-size, S22-replica-listener).\\\")\n        s['source_ids']=[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\",\\\"S22-replica-listener\\\"]\n        break\njson.dump(m,open('map.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nfb={\\\"ref_ids\\\":[\\\"1f0944699e7d4301909aa30f0523e9b5\\\",\\\"3ee262e5afd44c419b561c23376ffafb\\\",\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S38-client-command-size\\\",\\\"S22-replica-listener\\\"],\n \\\"answered\\\":\\\"The codec finding's three confirmed scenarios are recorded at its coordinates: the value truncation, the following command decoding to garbage in the same buffer, and the receiver-side decoder panic on a real PreAccept, together with the boundary the default configuration stays inside and the unread reader-side reaction. The codec surface's reason and sources were extended to match, so the map no longer describes only the first scenario.\\\",\n \\\"remaining\\\":[\\\"what a participant does with a stream displaced by the leftover bytes, which no check exercised\\\",\n   \\\"whether the client library caps the command size it builds\\\",\n   \\\"the structurally stuck scope issue on the superseded C1 artifact\\\"],\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Recording all three scenarios where the framing lives keeps the map consistent with the confirmed claim; the claim and its checks remain the home for the verdicts, and the unread reader-side item is stated rather than absorbed.\\\",\n \\\"understanding\\\":\\\"updated\\\",\\\"question_updates\\\":{}}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Map handoff aligning the codec entry with its three confirmed scenarios: one overview open detail and one existing surface reason updated, both sourced. No requirement, binding, edge or identity changes.\\\",\n \\\"map_path\\\":\\\"map.json\\\",\n \\\"map_changes\\\":{\n  \\\"core_overview\\\":{\\\"impact\\\":\\\"clarification\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The open detail for the codec now states all three confirmed consequences (truncated value, garbage following command, decoder panic) and the unread reader-side item.\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S22-replica-listener\\\"],\\\"preserves\\\":\\\"Formation, context, connection and the other open details are unchanged.\\\"},\n  \\\"surface:state/state.go value and command codec\\\":{\\\"impact\\\":\\\"clarification\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The surface's reason and sources were extended to the three confirmed scenarios so its summary is not limited to the first.\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S22-replica-listener\\\"],\\\"preserves\\\":\\\"The disposition (infrastructure) and the role of the codec as framing rather than protocol decision are unchanged.\\\"}},\n \\\"feedback\\\":fb}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-map-c10b.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-map-c10b.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
